module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.Affine.EtaleSite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.FormalSpectrum
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.SmallEtaleSite.McQuillanAffineEtale

/-!
# From the completions of the étale algebras to the affine étale site

Let `A` be a linearly topologized ring over a scheme `S` of a big fppf site, presented by a
quotient system, and let `J` be a weak ideal of definition of `A`, so that `Spec (A ⧸ J)` is an
affine object of the site. An object `B^∧` of the category of Stacks 0DEF — an étale ring map
`A → B` together with the completion `B^∧ = lim B/JB` — has a quotient stage `B ⧸ JB` at `J`,
and `Spec (B ⧸ JB)` is an affine object of the site étale over `Spec (A ⧸ J)`: it is of finite
type over `Spec (A ⧸ J)`, which bounds its size, and `A ⧸ J → B ⧸ JB` is étale by Stacks 0AN8.
The stage is functorial in the continuous `A`-algebra homomorphisms of the completions, so this
is a functor from the category of Stacks 0DEF to the opposite of the affine étale site of
`Spec (A ⧸ J)`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stage` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stageStr`: the quotient stage `B ⧸ JB` of an
  object of the category of Stacks 0DEF, and its structure map from `A ⧸ J`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stageHom`: the map of quotient stages induced
  by a continuous `A`-algebra homomorphism of the completions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stageObj`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stageProj` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stageObjMap`: the affine object
  `Spec (B ⧸ JB)` of the big fppf site of `S`, its étale projection to `Spec (A ⧸ J)`, and the
  functoriality in the completions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.completionAffineEtaleFunctor` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.completionAffineEtale`: **Stacks 0DEF**, the functor from the
  category of the completions to the opposite of the affine étale site of `Spec (A ⧸ J)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.etale_stageStr`: the structure map of a
  quotient stage is étale, which is Stacks 0AN8.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.contains_spec_stage`: the spectrum of a
  quotient stage satisfies the size cutoff of the site, so it is an object of it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stageHom_homOfAlgebraHom`: on a morphism coming
  from an `A`-algebra homomorphism of the underlying étale algebras, the induced map of quotient
  stages is the evident one, so the functor is not valued in a degenerate subcategory of
  morphisms.

## Implementation notes

A morphism of the category of Stacks 0DEF is a continuous `A`-algebra homomorphism
`g : B₁^∧ → B₂^∧` of the completions, not a homomorphism `B₁ → B₂` of the étale algebras, so the
induced map of quotient stages is not immediate. It is obtained from the kernels of the
projections: by Stacks 0AN6 the kernel of `B^∧ → B/JB` is the closure of the ideal generated by
`J`, and `g` carries that ideal of `B₁^∧` into the corresponding ideal of `B₂^∧` because it is a
homomorphism of `A`-algebras, hence carries its closure into the kernel of `B₂^∧ → B₂/JB₂`,
which is open and therefore closed. The projections are surjective, so the resulting map of
quotients is the unique one compatible with them; that characterization
(`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.EtaleCompletion.stageHom_projection`) is what proves
functoriality and `A`-linearity.

The affine étale site here is that of the stage `Spec (A ⧸ J)`, not that of the reduction of
`Spf A`: a reduction would have to be chosen from Stacks 0AIN, and the
comparison functor of Stacks 0DEE is likewise carried at an arbitrary affine object `V` of the
site with a morphism to the formal algebraic space
(`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.affineEtaleComparison`), the reduction entering only as data in
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.reductionAffineEtaleComparison`. Taking `V` to be the stage
`Spec (A ⧸ J)` and the morphism to be the stage inclusion into `Spf A`, the target of the
functor built here is literally the target of that comparison functor.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DEF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DEF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DEE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DEE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AN6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AN6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AN8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AN8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AIF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AIF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 000R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H01](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H01)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalRing

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

universe u

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [TopologicalSpace A]

namespace EtaleCompletion

/-! ### The quotient stages of an object of the category of Stacks 0DEF -/

/-- The quotient stage `B ⧸ JB` of an object `B^∧` of the category of Stacks 0DEF at a weak
ideal of definition `J` of `A`. -/
abbrev stage (Y : EtaleCompletion A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) : Type u :=
  Y.carrier ⧸ extendedIdeal Y.str J

/-- The projection `B^∧ → B ⧸ JB` of the completion onto one of its quotient stages. -/
abbrev projection (Y : EtaleCompletion A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    Y.completion →+* Y.stage J :=
  TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.projection Y.str J

/-- The structure map `A ⧸ J → B ⧸ JB` of a quotient stage. -/
abbrev stageStr (Y : EtaleCompletion A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    A ⧸ J.1 →+* Y.stage J :=
  Ideal.quotientMap (extendedIdeal Y.str J) Y.str Ideal.le_comap_map

/-- The structure map of a quotient stage is étale. This is Stacks 0AN8 for the étale ring map
underlying an object of the category of Stacks 0DEF. -/
theorem etale_stageStr (Y : EtaleCompletion A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    (Y.stageStr J).Etale :=
  TopologicalRing.etale_quotientMap_weakIdealOfDefinition Y.etale J

/-- Two ring homomorphisms out of a quotient stage agreeing on the image of the projection from
the completion are equal, that projection being surjective. -/
theorem hom_ext_projection {Y : EtaleCompletion A} {J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A}
    {W : Type*} [CommRing W] {f₁ f₂ : Y.stage J →+* W}
    (h : ∀ x : Y.completion, f₁ (Y.projection J x) = f₂ (Y.projection J x)) : f₁ = f₂ :=
  RingHom.ext fun y ↦ by
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.projection_surjective Y.str J y
    exact h x

/-- A morphism of the category of Stacks 0DEF carries the kernel of the projection of its source
into the kernel of the projection of its target: that kernel is the closure of the ideal
generated by `J`, the morphism is a homomorphism of `A`-algebras, and the kernel of the target
projection is open, hence closed. -/
theorem ker_projection_le_comap {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    RingHom.ker (Y.projection J) ≤ Ideal.comap g.toRingHom (RingHom.ker (Z.projection J)) := by
  have hclosed : IsClosed
      (Ideal.comap g.toRingHom (RingHom.ker (Z.projection J)) : Set Y.completion) :=
    ((RingHom.ker (Z.projection J)).toAddSubgroup.isClosed_of_isOpen
      (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.isOpen_ker_projection Z.str J)).preimage
        g.continuous_toRingHom
  have hle : (J.1 : Ideal A) ≤
      Ideal.comap Y.structureMap (Ideal.comap g.toRingHom (RingHom.ker (Z.projection J))) := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_comap, g.comp_structureMap]
    exact TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.le_comap_ker_projection Z.str J
  rw [TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.ker_projection_eq_closure]
  exact closure_minimal (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr hle) hclosed

/-- The map of quotient stages `B₁ ⧸ JB₁ → B₂ ⧸ JB₂` induced by a morphism of the category of
Stacks 0DEF, that is by a continuous `A`-algebra homomorphism `B₁^∧ → B₂^∧`. -/
noncomputable def stageHom {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) : Y.stage J →+* Z.stage J :=
  (((Z.projection J).quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
      (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.projection_surjective Z.str J) :
        Z.completion ⧸ RingHom.ker (Z.projection J) ≃+* Z.stage J) : _ →+* Z.stage J).comp
    ((Ideal.quotientMap (RingHom.ker (Z.projection J)) g.toRingHom
        (ker_projection_le_comap g J)).comp
      ((((Y.projection J).quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
          (TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.projection_surjective Y.str J)).symm :
        Y.stage J ≃+* Y.completion ⧸ RingHom.ker (Y.projection J)) : _ →+* _))

/-- The induced map of quotient stages is compatible with the projections from the completions,
which characterizes it. -/
theorem stageHom_projection {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) (x : Y.completion) :
    stageHom g J (Y.projection J x) = Z.projection J (g.toRingHom x) := by
  unfold stageHom
  rw [RingHom.comp_apply, RingHom.comp_apply, RingHom.coe_coe, RingHom.coe_coe,
    RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_symm_apply, Ideal.quotientMap_mk]
  rfl

/-- The identity induces the identity map of quotient stages. -/
theorem stageHom_id (Y : EtaleCompletion A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    stageHom (𝟙 Y) J = RingHom.id (Y.stage J) :=
  hom_ext_projection fun x ↦ stageHom_projection (𝟙 Y) J x

/-- The induced map of quotient stages is compatible with composition. -/
theorem stageHom_comp {Y Z W : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z) (h : Z ⟶ W)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    stageHom (g ≫ h) J = (stageHom h J).comp (stageHom g J) :=
  hom_ext_projection fun x ↦
    calc stageHom (g ≫ h) J (Y.projection J x)
        = W.projection J (h.toRingHom (g.toRingHom x)) := stageHom_projection (g ≫ h) J x
      _ = stageHom h J (Z.projection J (g.toRingHom x)) :=
            (stageHom_projection h J (g.toRingHom x)).symm
      _ = (stageHom h J).comp (stageHom g J) (Y.projection J x) :=
            congrArg (stageHom h J) (stageHom_projection g J x).symm

/-- The induced map of quotient stages is a homomorphism of `A ⧸ J`-algebras. -/
theorem stageHom_comp_stageStr {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    (stageHom g J).comp (Y.stageStr J) = Z.stageStr J :=
  Ideal.Quotient.ringHom_ext (RingHom.ext fun a ↦
    calc stageHom g J (Y.projection J (Y.structureMap a))
        = Z.projection J (g.toRingHom (Y.structureMap a)) :=
          stageHom_projection g J (Y.structureMap a)
      _ = Z.projection J (Z.structureMap a) :=
          congrArg (Z.projection J) (RingHom.congr_fun g.comp_structureMap a))

/-- On a morphism induced by an `A`-algebra homomorphism of the underlying étale algebras, the
induced map of quotient stages is the map `B₁ ⧸ JB₁ → B₂ ⧸ JB₂` that homomorphism induces. -/
theorem stageHom_homOfAlgebraHom {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (φ : Y.carrier →+* Z.carrier)
    (hφ : φ.comp Y.str = Z.str) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    stageHom (homOfAlgebraHom φ hφ) J = stageMap φ hφ J :=
  hom_ext_projection fun x ↦ stageHom_projection (homOfAlgebraHom φ hφ) J x

/-! ### The affine étale charts attached to the quotient stages -/

/-- The spectrum of the structure map of a quotient stage is an étale morphism of schemes. -/
theorem etale_spec_stageStr (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) (Y : EtaleCompletion A) :
    Etale (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Y.stageStr J))) :=
  HasRingHomProperty.Spec_iff.mpr (Y.etale_stageStr J)

/-- On spectra, the induced map of quotient stages sits over `Spec (A ⧸ J)`. -/
theorem spec_stageHom_comp {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (stageHom g J)) ≫
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Y.stageStr J)) =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Z.stageStr J)) := by
  rw [← Spec.map_comp, ← CommRingCat.ofHom_comp, stageHom_comp_stageStr]

section Geometry

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- The spectrum of a quotient stage satisfies the size cutoff of the big fppf site, so it is an
object of it: it is the spectrum of a finite type algebra over `A ⧸ J`, whose spectrum is an
object of the site, and Stacks 000R (9)(b) bounds the size of such a spectrum. -/
theorem contains_spec_stage (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) (Y : EtaleCompletion A) :
    B.Contains (Spec (.of (Y.stage J))) := by
  let _ : Algebra (A ⧸ J.1) (Y.stage J) := (Y.stageStr J).toAlgebra
  have _ : Algebra.Etale (A ⧸ J.1) (Y.stage J) := Y.etale_stageStr J
  exact Scheme.size_Spec_lt_of_finiteType B.aleph0_lt_cutoff B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit
    (A ⧸ J.1) (Y.stage J) (D.inSite J)

/-- The object `Spec (B ⧸ JB)` of the big fppf site of `S`, with the structure morphism to `S`
it inherits from the stage `Spec (A ⧸ J)` of the quotient system. -/
noncomputable def stageObj (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A)
    (Y : EtaleCompletion A) : BigFppfOver B S hS :=
  Over.mk (ObjectProperty.homMk
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Y.stageStr J)) ≫ D.overS J) :
      B.obj (contains_spec_stage B S hS D J Y) ⟶ B.obj hS)

/-- The projection `Spec (B ⧸ JB) ⟶ Spec (A ⧸ J)` in the big fppf site of `S`. -/
noncomputable def stageProj (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A)
    (Y : EtaleCompletion A) :
    stageObj B S hS D J Y ⟶ (BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj (D.stage J) :=
  Over.homMk (ObjectProperty.homMk (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Y.stageStr J))))
    (by apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext; rfl)

/-- The projection of a quotient stage to `Spec (A ⧸ J)` is étale. -/
theorem etale_toScheme_stageProj (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) (Y : EtaleCompletion A) :
    Etale ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (stageProj B S hS D J Y)) :=
  etale_spec_stageStr J Y

/-- The morphism of the big fppf site of `S` induced on the objects `Spec (B ⧸ JB)` by a
morphism of the category of Stacks 0DEF. -/
noncomputable def stageObjMap (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A)
    {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    stageObj B S hS D J Z ⟶ stageObj B S hS D J Y :=
  Over.homMk (ObjectProperty.homMk (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (stageHom g J))))
    (by
      apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
      change Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (stageHom g J)) ≫
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Y.stageStr J)) ≫ D.overS J) =
        Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Z.stageStr J)) ≫ D.overS J
      rw [← Category.assoc, spec_stageHom_comp])

/-- The induced morphism of objects of the site lies over `Spec (A ⧸ J)`. -/
theorem stageObjMap_comp_stageProj (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) {Y Z : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    stageObjMap B S hS D J g ≫ stageProj B S hS D J Y = stageProj B S hS D J Z :=
  Over.OverMorphism.ext (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (spec_stageHom_comp g J))

/-- The identity induces the identity morphism of objects of the site. -/
theorem stageObjMap_id (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A)
    (Y : EtaleCompletion A) : stageObjMap B S hS D J (𝟙 Y) = 𝟙 _ := by
  refine Over.OverMorphism.ext (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ ?_)
  simp [stageObjMap, stageHom_id]
  rfl

/-- The induced morphism of objects of the site is contravariantly compatible with
composition. -/
theorem stageObjMap_comp (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A) (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A)
    {Y Z W : EtaleCompletion A} (g : Y ⟶ Z) (h : Z ⟶ W) :
    stageObjMap B S hS D J (g ≫ h) = stageObjMap B S hS D J h ≫ stageObjMap B S hS D J g := by
  refine Over.OverMorphism.ext (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ ?_)
  simp [stageObjMap, stageHom_comp]
  rfl

end Geometry

end EtaleCompletion

/-! ### Stacks 0DEF: the functor to the affine étale site -/

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **Stacks 0DEF**, the functor from the opposite of the category of the completions `B^∧` to
the affine étale site of the stage `Spec (A ⧸ J)`. On objects it is `B^∧ ↦ Spec (B ⧸ JB)`, which
is an affine object of the site étale over `Spec (A ⧸ J)` by Stacks 0AN8 and Stacks 000R; on
morphisms it is the map of quotient stages induced by a continuous `A`-algebra homomorphism of
the completions. -/
noncomputable def completionAffineEtaleFunctor (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    (EtaleCompletion A)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Space.AffineEtale B S hS
      (yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj (D.stage J))) where
  obj Y :=
    ⟨⟨CostructuredArrow.mk (yoneda.map (EtaleCompletion.stageProj B S hS D J Y.unop)),
      isEtaleChart_yoneda_map B S hS _
        (EtaleCompletion.etale_toScheme_stageProj B S hS D J Y.unop)⟩,
      inferInstanceAs (IsAffine (Spec (.of (Y.unop.stage J))))⟩
  map {Y Z} g :=
    ObjectProperty.homMk (ObjectProperty.homMk (CostructuredArrow.homMk
      (EtaleCompletion.stageObjMap B S hS D J g.unop)
      (by rw [CostructuredArrow.mk_hom_eq_self, CostructuredArrow.mk_hom_eq_self,
            ← Functor.map_comp, EtaleCompletion.stageObjMap_comp_stageProj])))
  map_id Y := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    refine CostructuredArrow.hom_ext _ _ ?_
    exact EtaleCompletion.stageObjMap_id B S hS D J Y.unop
  map_comp {Y Z W} g h := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    refine CostructuredArrow.hom_ext _ _ ?_
    exact EtaleCompletion.stageObjMap_comp B S hS D J h.unop g.unop

/-- **Stacks 0DEF**, the functor from the category of the `A`-algebras `B^∧ = lim B/JB` of its
items (1) and (2) to the *opposite* of an affine étale site, which is the direction in which
Stacks 0DEF identifies that category with `(X_{affine,étale})^{opp}`. It sends an étale ring map
`A → B` to the affine object `Spec (B ⧸ JB)` of the site, étale over `Spec (A ⧸ J)`, and a
continuous `A`-algebra homomorphism `B₁^∧ → B₂^∧` to the morphism `Spec (B₂ ⧸ JB₂) ⟶
Spec (B₁ ⧸ JB₁)` it induces on quotient stages.

The site is the affine étale site of the stage `Spec (A ⧸ J)`, which is the target of the
comparison functor `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.affineEtaleComparison` of Stacks 0DEE at the
affine object `Spec (A ⧸ J)` of the site and the stage inclusion `Spec (A ⧸ J) ⟶ Spf A`. -/
@[stacks 0DEF "the functor from the category of the completions `B^∧` of its items (1) and (2) \
to the opposite of an affine étale site, on objects the quotient stage `B^∧ ↦ Spec (B ⧸ JB)` \
and on morphisms the map of quotient stages a continuous `A`-algebra homomorphism of \
completions induces. The site is the affine étale site of the stage `Spec (A ⧸ J)`, the target \
of this library's Stacks 0DEE comparison functor at that affine object, rather than of the \
reduction of `Spf A`, which would have to be chosen from Stacks 0AIN. The functor is not \
shown to be \
an equivalence: the quasi-inverse would have to make `Spf B^∧ ⟶ Spf A` representable étale, \
which needs Stacks 0AKN and the locality on the target of the universe-lifted representability \
and étaleness conditions, neither of which this library carries"]
noncomputable def completionAffineEtale (D : QuotientSystem B S hS A)
    (J : WeakIdealOfDefinitionIndex A) :
    EtaleCompletion A ⥤ (Space.AffineEtale B S hS
      (yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj (D.stage J))))ᵒᵖ :=
  (completionAffineEtaleFunctor B S hS D J).rightOp

end AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

end
